<title>ITALY: ATHLETICS-ETHIOPIANS DUBE WINS ROME MARATHON.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-ETHIOPIANS DUBE WINS ROME MARATHON.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ethiopia's Jillo Dube won the Rome City Marathon in two hours 13 minutes four seconds, finishing in the shadow of the ancient Colosseum ahead of compatriot Moges Taye and Kenyan Kiprop Cheruyot.</p>
<p>Estonia's Jane Salumae won the women's race, ahead of Italy's Anna Villani and Ukraine's Irina Sklyarenko.</p>
